# labwc autostart for the Segno floor console.
# Copied to ~/.config/labwc/autostart. Runs once when labwc starts.
#
# Order matters: pin the displays deterministically FIRST (so the 16" is the
# primary main-UI output and the 7" is the waveform output at a known position),
# then launch the app full-screen. The app opens its waveform second window,
# which the compositor places on the secondary output.

# Pin outputs by connector name (idempotent; safe to re-run).
"$HOME/segno/deploy/rpi/pin-displays.sh" &

# Launch the Segno release bundle full-screen. Adjust the path to your build
# output. Build it with console/kiosk mode on so the on-screen toolbar is
# hidden (pedals drive it): flutter build linux --release
#   --target lib/main_production.dart --dart-define=SEGNO_CONSOLE=true
#   (see deploy/rpi/README.md).
SEGNO_BIN="${SEGNO_BIN:-$HOME/segno/build/linux/arm64/release/bundle/segno}"

# Launch under pw-jack so the engine's preferred JACK backend binds to
# PipeWire's JACK server. Without it the real libjack is loaded, finds no
# running jackd, and the engine hangs retrying — audio silently dies on boot
# with no terminal to see it (needs the `pipewire-jack` package; verified on a
# Pi 4B bring-up). Falls back to a direct launch if pw-jack is not installed.
SEGNO_LAUNCH=""
command -v pw-jack >/dev/null 2>&1 && SEGNO_LAUNCH="pw-jack"
exec $SEGNO_LAUNCH "$SEGNO_BIN" &
